## Make on-behalf-of data-plane clients use the caller's token

Context: In Databricks Apps mode `DatabricksAuth` preferred the app's
service-principal credentials over an explicit token. So
`get_data_plane_client(token=<forwarded user token>)` authenticated as the
app, and Unity Catalog grants were checked for the app, not the user. Query
history on a deployed app showed every "user" read executed by the app SP.
Reported as found-but-not-fixed in #235.

Changes:
1. src/back/core/databricks/DatabricksAuth.py
   `on_behalf_of=True` makes the explicit token win; new `uses_app_credentials` replaces four inline checks.
2. src/back/core/databricks/DatabricksClient.py, SQLWarehouse.py
   Pass the flag through; kernel reconnect uses `uses_app_credentials`.
3. src/back/core/helpers/DatabricksHelpers.py
   `get_data_plane_client` sets `on_behalf_of=True`.

Modified files:
- src/back/core/databricks/DatabricksAuth.py
- src/back/core/databricks/DatabricksClient.py
- src/back/core/databricks/SQLWarehouse.py
